{%- doc -%}
  SYPerformance badge.

  Only SYPerformance's own parts get the accent colour. That distinction is the
  point of the badge system, so do not reuse `in-house` for anything else.

  THE ONE COPY RULE (2026-08-26): SYPerformance IS the manufacturer — it owns the
  designs, drawings and specs, contracts production to them, inspects and
  warranties. Say manufacturer, we make, we build, our parts. Never name a shop
  floor: no "machined in our own shop", "cut here", "on our machines". The first
  is true and unshakeable; the second is checkable and not ours to claim.

  @param {string} label - Badge text. Rendered uppercase by CSS.
  @param {string} [variant] - in-house | built-to-order | in-stock | sold-out | sale

  @example
  {% render 'syp-badge', label: 'SYPerformance', variant: 'in-house' %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign badge_classes = 'syp-badge'
  if variant != blank
    assign badge_classes = badge_classes | append: ' syp-badge--' | append: variant
  endif
-%}

<span class="{{ badge_classes }}">{{ label }}</span>
